MKDIR(1)                     Funny CLI Manual                     MKDIR(1)

NAME
    mkdir — Create a directory, because empty space has to start somewhere.

SYNOPSIS
    mkdir <dir>

DESCRIPTION
    The mkdir command creates a new directory at the specified path.

    Parent directories are created automatically if they do not already
    exist.

    If the specified directory already exists, mkdir refuses to overwrite
    it and reports that it already exists.

USAGE
    > mkdir <dir>       # Creates the specified directory.

FUN FACTS
    - mkdir stands for "make directory".
    - It can create an entire chain of missing parent directories.
    - Creating a directory is considerably safer than deleting one.
    - Empty directories are full of possibilities.

EXAMPLES
    > mkdir documents
        Creates a new directory called documents.

    > mkdir projects/python
        Creates both projects and python if they do not already exist.

    > mkdir /home/user/my_project
        Creates my_project inside /home/user.

    > mkdir documents
        Reports an error if documents already exists.

